---
// Support page. The App Store listing and the app both publish this URL as the
// place to get help (PATHS_SUPPORT_URL), so it has to answer without a login.
// Written from what the app actually does: Apple handles billing, account
// deletion is in Profile > Settings, blocking is in the crew, the Watch is fed
// by the phone, and proof links are signed and expire.
//
// The contact address is support@particlesofmind.com, the same address the
// in-app Report button mails and clause 19 of the Terms names.
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
---

<Layout title="Support" description="How to get help with Paths, and answers to the questions that come up most.">
  <LegalPage title="Support">
    <span slot="updated">8 November 2026</span>

    <p>
      Paths is a habit app for iPhone, iPad and Apple Watch. If something is wrong, or you cannot find an answer
      below, write to <a href="mailto:support@particlesofmind.com">support@particlesofmind.com</a> and you will get a
      reply within <mark>[TO CONFIRM: response time, e.g. two working days]</mark>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="account">I cannot sign in</h2>
    <p>
      Tap <strong>Forgot password</strong> on the sign-in screen. The reset link is sent to the address on the account
      and expires after an hour; ask for a new one if it does. If the address itself is wrong or unreachable, write to
      support from any address and say which username is affected.
    </p>

    <h2 id="subscription">Billing, cancelling and refunds</h2>
    <p>
      Subscriptions are bought through Apple, not through us, so they are managed in
      <strong>Settings &rsaquo; your name &rsaquo; Subscriptions</strong> on your device. Cancelling there stops the
      next renewal and leaves the plan running until the period you have paid for ends.
    </p>
    <p>
      Refunds are Apple's to give: ask at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>. We
      cannot issue them, and we cannot see your payment details.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Deleting your Paths account does not cancel a subscription bought through Apple.</strong> Cancel it in
      Settings as well, or it keeps renewing.
    </p>

    <h2 id="delete">Deleting your account and your data</h2>
    <p>
      In the app: <strong>Profile &rsaquo; Settings &rsaquo; Delete account</strong>. This removes your profile, your
      patterns, the proof you uploaded, your crew membership and your messages. It cannot be undone, and it is not
      reversible by writing to support afterwards.
    </p>
    <p>To take a copy with you first, use <strong>Download my data</strong> on the same screen.</p>

    <h2 id="reporting">Reporting someone, or blocking them</h2>
    <p>
      Touch and hold a message or a member in your crew. <strong>Report</strong> sends it to us for review.
      <strong>Block member</strong> removes everything that member posts or says from your feed straight away; the
      blocked list is on the crew's info screen, and a block can be undone there.
    </p>
    <p>
      Anything urgent, or anything involving a minor or a threat, goes to
      <a href="mailto:support@particlesofmind.com">support@particlesofmind.com</a> with "urgent" in the subject.
    </p>

    <h2 id="watch">The Watch app is not showing today's patterns</h2>
    <p>
      Open Paths on the iPhone once with the Watch nearby: the Watch is sent the day's patterns from the phone, and it
      cannot fetch them on its own. If the list is still empty, check that Paths is installed on the Watch in the
      iPhone's Watch app, and that both devices are on the same day's date.
    </p>

    <h2 id="proof">A photo or recording I submitted will not open</h2>
    <p>
      Proof is stored privately and the app signs a fresh link each time it shows one. A link that has been open on
      screen for over an hour can expire; tap <strong>Retry image</strong>, or leave the screen and come back.
    </p>

    <h2 id="privacy">Privacy and terms</h2>
    <p>
      What we collect and why is in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. The rules for using Paths are in the
      <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>.
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
